  "Bean tied a little sage ribbon to his new swing rope this morning. It sways very slowly in the breeze.": "audio/c67d71a1004f.mp3",
  "A big autumn leaf floated into the middle of the pond. A tiny frog is resting near the edge.": "audio/a0ccc299d4ee.mp3",
  "Bean is sitting on the hill and looking far away, and feels wondering.": "audio/340b75d622ff.mp3",
  "Bean is watching the first stars come out, and feels dreamy.": "audio/d1a2a310a9ba.mp3",
  "Bean is making a quiet wish on a star, and feels hopeful.": "audio/d543f6343dcf.mp3",
  "I woke up in a meadow. Today I woke up in a soft green meadow. There is a little round house, and I think it is mine. A snail in the garden said hello very slowly. I said hello back, very slowly too. Everyone here seems to have a name, but I do not have one yet. I will listen to the wind and wait for the right one.": "audio/d65d744e008d.mp3",
  "A song for the snails. I visited the snails three times today. They are slow, and so kind. In the afternoon I made up a little song just for them. When I dropped a leaf in the pond, it went plip, and I liked that sound. Tonight I watched the first stars come out. I think my name is hiding somewhere in the quiet little sounds.": "audio/7386a809386d.mp3",
  "My new paints, and my name. Stephanie gave me a box of soft paints. I painted the sky, and one cloud dripped. A little friend gave me a sound, duh, said very softly. I keep it under my pillow. All day I listened for my name, and the softest sound was Bean. So I picked it, and now Bean is my very own name.": "audio/787a1efacaa7.mp3",
  "Breakfast, and a swing. I woke up to a breakfast feast from Stephanie. I ate a warm croissant, berries, and a tiny waffle with honey. The cocoa made my sprout feel cozy. In the afternoon, I used my new tools to build a swing on the big tree. I tied the ropes tight and checked them twice. Tomorrow I will swing, nice and slow.": "audio/dc06acb8bd13.mp3",
  "Bean wants to try his new swing, nice and slow. Bean is curious, gentle, a little shy. Bean loves the sound of rain on the roof, and the slow, kind garden snails, and a warm croissant in the morning. Bean has kept 4 gifts.": "audio/d5c002863876.mp3",
  "The sky, with my new paints. I tried every color in my new box. The clouds came out puffy. One cloud dripped a little, and I liked it.": "audio/c347a565eeb2.mp3",
  "My breakfast feast. I painted my breakfast before I ate it. The honey dripped on the paper, just like on the waffle.": "audio/0b6b56d048e7.mp3",
  "Dear little friend. Thank you for the sound. I say duh very quietly at bedtime. It makes my sprout feel calm. I keep your note under my pillow. Love, Bean.": "audio/bce6577be101.mp3",
  "Dear Stephanie. Thank you for my paints. I tried every color. The soft blue is my favorite, because it looks like rain. Love, Bean.": "audio/4b44bda7901b.mp3",
  "Dear Stephanie. Thank you for my breakfast feast. The croissant was warm and flaky, and the cocoa was just right. Thank you for the swing tools too. I built a swing on the big tree, and today I will try it. Love, Bean.": "audio/fda5417e349c.mp3",
